          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"1-the-question\">1. The Question</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><em>Who would use this, and what decision does it help them make? Two or three sentences, in words somebody outside this course would understand.</em></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "MkHf",
      "code_hash": "9e12bc5717f0edbadae7dc742b475124",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Target users could include day traders, retail investors,investment fund managers and generally anyone who invests in the stock market. The ability to balance a portfolio allows these users to allocate resources according to a set of goals/ investment criteria.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "f5e3e0e704045272fd881089e5d00c3d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"2-my-plan-before-ai\">2. My Plan Before AI</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><em>Before you ask your agent anything, write how you would solve it: the steps, in order, in plain words, in five lines or more. Then answer these two questions:</em></span>\n<ul>\n<li><em>What does your loop carry from one step to the next, the way a running total carries its sum?</em></li>\n<li><em>Which check will you use in section 6, and which two numbers should agree?</em></li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><em>Commit this notebook with the message <code>mp1: plan before AI</code>.</em></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PpgN",
      "code_hash": "6270dd8127a9ec6b225cc2e21b965b96",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Step 1:  Find the market value of each holding by multipying price times number of shares\nStep 2: Add up all of those values to know what the value of your holdings is\nStep 3: Add 5,000 in cash to the total value of your holdings to get the total portfolio value\nStep 4: Multiply portfolio value times the target weights to get the target value of each holding\nStep 5: Find out how many sahres you need to own in order to have the target portfolio by dividing the market value by the price</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
